tps://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-19T04:44:40Z","updated_at":"2025-07-19T04:44:40Z","body":"> Any minimal project to make testing this easier?\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/beicause/godot-cpp-template/tree/test-class-icon","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3091593989/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092563016","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108607#issuecomment-3092563016","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108607","id":3092563016,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64VMRI","user":{"login":"sylbeth","id":102521501,"node_id":"U_kgDOBhxanQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102521501?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth","html_url":"https://github.com/sylbeth","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-19T20:46:07Z","updated_at":"2025-07-19T21:22:27Z","body":"I am not sure it supersedes my implementation, it seems more like a parallel functionality. From what I take from the code, is that you take the parent class, and use that icon, right? I didn't go this route because I was told it wasn't possible back when I implemented this, but that would've been a previous default. Correct me if I'm wrong, reading Godot code feels like a puzzle most times, but I don't think your pr gives the user the ability to use the icon \"Sprite3D\" on a subclass of \"CharacterBody2D\", and that was indeed my intention. I find most times I don't want to just use the superclass icon, but an icon that best represents the new class I'm making, and I always find myself having to go through `godot/editor/icons`, choose an icon, copy and paste. I believe the algorithm should work like this:\r\n\r\n- If path to icon provided\r\n  - If icon exists, use icon\r\n  - If icon doesn't exist, but has the same name as an editor icon, use that\r\n  - If none of that works, treat the path as nonexistent\r\n- In case it doesn't exist, or if the previous step failed\r\n  - Use superclass if found\r\n  - Use default fallback otherwise\r\n\r\nI suggest we work together to implement this algorithm to cover all of it in one go, if you'd want, otherwise you can do it or I can do it","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092563016/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3093197336","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108607#issuecomment-3093197336","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108607","id":3093197336,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64XnIY","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-20T04:39:16Z","updated_at":"2025-07-20T04:39:16Z","body":"Yes, I believe this PR is compatible with yours.\r\n\r\nIn my opinion automatically using the parent class icon is sufficient. Exposing the editor icons means additional compatibility burden. I'm not sure if it's actually useful.\r\n\r\nIf you want to implement that, I think you can make the changes in `extension_class_get_icon`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3093197336/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3093204848","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108607#issuecomment-3093204848","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108607","id":3093204848,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64Xo9w","user":{"login":"sylbeth","id":102521501,"node_id":"U_kgDOBhxanQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102521501?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth","html_url":"https://github.com/sylbeth","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sylbeth/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-20T04:58:19Z","updated_at":"2025-07-20T04:58:19Z","body":"I did implement it in my PR, so it's just matching both codes.\n\nIn any case, yes, it is really useful. If I make a Node that represents a Ball, I'm going to be using Sphere3D instead of probably anything I've inherited, it gives better visual information.\n\nPlus, I believe it's needed for feature parity with GDScript, since GDExtension should be a first class citizen of Godot.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3093204848/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":